---
description: Code style and formatting for C/C++ embedded projects
globs: *.cpp, *.h, *.ino, *.c
alwaysApply: false
---

# Naming
- Functions and variables: lowerCamelCase (`readSensorValue`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE or kCamelCase for constexpr (`MAX_RETRIES`)
- Classes/structs: UpperCamelCase (`TemperatureSensor`)
- Pin definitions grouped at the top of the file with clear names
  (`constexpr uint8_t PIN_RELAY = 5;`)

# Structure
- One responsibility per function; functions longer than ~40 lines get split
- Header guards or `#pragma once` in every header
- setup(): initialization only; loop(): dispatching only – logic lives in
  dedicated functions/classes
- Group related configuration in a config section or config.h

# Comments
- Comments in German, explain WHY not WHAT
- Every non-obvious timing value, buffer size, or magic constant gets a
  short justification comment
- Mark workarounds clearly: `// WORKAROUND: <reason, date>`

# Types
- Fixed-width types for protocol/hardware data: `uint8_t`, `uint32_t` etc.
- `bool` for flags, never `int`
- `const`/`constexpr` wherever possible; pointers const-correct
- No implicit narrowing conversions – cast explicitly and justify
